Create User 
Information related to cluster is stored in the kube/config 
# ~/.kube/config
1. first we should generate the users private key 
#openssl genrsa -out pavan.key 2048
then we must create a certificate signing request for the user with the key 
this command generate certifcate signning request 
#openssl req -new pavan.key  -out pavan.csr -subj "/CN=pavan/O=dev/O=example.org
CN stands for common name , it act like username 
O act like group name , we can give multiple groups to the current user 
-out pavan.csr = storing certificate signing request to the current folder 

Now the private key and certificate siging request are ready 
#ls | grep pavan 
Now this certificate siging request must be signed by the certificate authority 
they can get the certificate authority details from kubeconfig file 

to sign it , to generate this command

#openssl x509 -req -CA ~/.minikube/ca.crt -CAkey ~/.minikube/ca.key -CAcreateserial -days 730 -in pavan.csr  -out pavan.crt

in Kube/config file 
cluster:
  certificate-authority:/Users/pavan.elthepu/.minikube/ca.crt


we should add the user to the cluster with kubectl config set-credentials
#kubectl config set-credentails pavan --client-certificate=pavan.crt --client-key=pavan-kay

then , we should create a context for thsi user 
#kubectl config set-context pavan-minikube --cluster=minikube --user=pavan --namespace=default 
veriffy context 
#kkubectl config get-contexts
switch the context 
#kubectl config use-context pavan-minikube 


we should try to give permisions to the users 
in kubernate , we can give the permisions to a user with roles and rolebinding 
this is simple role monifiest file 
apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata;
  name: pod-reader
rules:
  - apiGroup: [""] #"" indicates the core API group 
    verbs: ["get","watch","list"]
    resources: ["pods","pods/log"]

#kubectl apply -f role.yaml

Now User and ROle both are ready , now connect bothso that user will be having these permissions 
In ROleBinding we connect both subject and Role 
this subject can be user or usergroup or even a service account 
and role we defined what we can access and what we cannot access when we attach the subject and roll with RoleBinding we are attaching the permissions to the user 




